      "content": "but i've heard that the omeprazole actually builds up a layer of protection so it makes it okay to take stuff like advil. i just want to get through this weekend without losing my mind from the tooth pain. if i take a standard dose of advil, like 200mg or 400mg, is that actually going to cause an ulcer or something immediately? it feels like you're being super cautious and i just need a straight answer on whether a small dose is dangerous or not.",
